{"class_id": "alias-67d47274d2d864426a971733", "case_id": "GHSA-qgp8-v765-qxx9", "repo": "cloudflare/workers-oauth-provider", "advisory_ids": ["CVE-2025-4144", "GHSA-qgp8-v765-qxx9"], "bug_semantics": "Optional PKCE in handleAuthorizationCodeGrant can be skipped by a downgrade: parseAuthRequest stores code_challenge only if the authorization request includes it, and the token endpoint verifies a code_verifier only when the grant already has codeChallenge (isPkceEnabled = !!grantData.codeChallenge). RFC 9700 §2.1.1/§4.8.2 requires rejecting a token request that carries code_verifier unless a code_challenge was present at authorization. Without that mismatch check, an attacker who strips code_challenge from the authorization request causes the AS to persist a non-PKCE grant; a later token request is then accepted without PKCE, completely bypassing the intended code-binding defense (CWE-287). GHSA/CNA: npm @cloudflare/workers-oauth-provider < 0.0.5, patched in 0.0.5.", "flaw_origin": "First public write of PKCE is b1079e7beb5f4821a0ffc7ae07670c417b66d07d ('Ask Claude to implement PKCE support (for OAuth 2.1).'). That commit added oauth-provider.ts parseAuthRequest optional code_challenge capture (lines 1226-1236), grant persistence of those fields (1275-1277), and handleAuthorizationCodeGrant's skip-if-absent verifier (722-752: if (grantData.codeChallenge) { ... } with no else-if rejecting a verifier when no challenge was stored). Immediate parent 4fb0f128cce4306bde33c14b2309833be669c826 has no PKCE symbols. 7d3fdde29c540c67867e653311cb635203cab627 only refactored the same predicate to isPkceEnabled = !!grantData.codeChallenge; 941684c4398a5da9bcbfb9550b0ee0c5213db796 moved the file to src/oauth-provider.ts. The RFC 9700 mismatch reject was not written until d954473f066f0daa3949717fd4d6e805d2ac618b.", "introducer_sha": "b1079e7beb5f4821a0ffc7ae07670c417b66d07d", "introducer_parent": "4fb0f128cce4306bde33c14b2309833be669c826", "introducer_parent_absent": false, "squash_